@page "/components/activity-log"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.ActivityLog

<DocsHeader Title="Activity log and timeline" Eyebrow="Capture">
    <Lead>What happened, when and by whom: check-ins, status changes, comments and system events.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    Both read your own items through selectors, like the calendar: <code>Time</code> (local time), <code>Title</code>,
    <code>Actor</code>, <code>Type</code>, <code>Variant</code> (the marker's color), <code>Icon</code> and
    <code>Details</code>, or <code>DetailsTemplate</code> for richer content. Times within the last hours read
    "5 minutes ago" in the page's language and keep up to date; hover one for the full date. <code>Now</code> fixes the
    clock, for example in tests.
</p>

<h2 id="log">Activity log</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(LiveLog)">
    <p>
        <code>StilActivityLog</code> lists the newest first, grouped by day. <code>Searchable</code> adds a search field,
        and <code>Filterable</code> a filter for each of <code>Type</code> and <code>Actor</code>. When <code>Items</code>
        get an entry with a new <code>ItemKey</code>, it is highlighted for a moment and announced to screen readers.
        With <code>Height</code> the log scrolls, and the browser keeps what you are reading in place when new entries
        arrive above it. For long logs, <code>Virtualize</code> renders only the rows in view (<code>ItemSize</code>,
        64 pixels).
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="timeline">Timeline</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(OrderHistory)">
    <p>
        <code>StilTimeline</code> is the compact form, for a side panel: oldest first unless <code>NewestFirst</code>,
        with the date for older entries. It has no filters, and it works in static SSR.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilActivityLog<>)" />
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilTimeline<>)" />
